&lt;p&gt;**Time Limit:**6000MS **Memory Limit:**524288KB &lt;strong&gt;64bit IO Format:&lt;/strong&gt;%I64d &amp;amp; %I64u&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Submit &lt;a href="http://acm.hust.edu.cn/vjudge/contest/view.action?cid=96696#status//B/0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;Status&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="http://acm.hust.edu.cn/vjudge/problem/viewProblem.action?id=261053" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;Practice&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="http://acm.hust.edu.cn/vjudge/problem/visitOriginUrl.action?id=261053" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;CodeForces 589B&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Description&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dasha decided to bake a big and tasty layer cake. In order to do that she went shopping and bought &lt;em&gt;n&lt;/em&gt; rectangular cake layers. The length and the width of the &lt;em&gt;i&lt;/em&gt;-th cake layer were &lt;em&gt;a__i&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;b__i&lt;/em&gt; respectively, while the height of each cake layer was equal to one.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>codeforces 589 D - Boulevard</title><link>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-10-26-codeforces589d-boulevard/</link><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2015 13:55:00 +0000</pubDate><author>hust.111qqz@gmail.com (111qqz)</author><guid>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-10-26-codeforces589d-boulevard/</guid><description/></item><item><title>codeforces #324 div 2 A. Olesya and Rodion</title><link>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-10-11-codeforces23324div2a-olesyaandrodion/</link><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2015 15:53:00 +0000</pubDate><author>hust.111qqz@gmail.com (111qqz)</author><guid>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-10-11-codeforces23324div2a-olesyaandrodion/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A. Olesya and Rodion&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;time limit per test&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1 second&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;memory limit per test&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;256 megabytes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;input&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;standard input&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;output&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;standard output&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Olesya loves numbers consisting of &lt;em&gt;n&lt;/em&gt; digits, and Rodion only likes numbers that are divisible by &lt;em&gt;t&lt;/em&gt;. Find some number that satisfies both of them.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>[转自codeforces] How to come up with the solutions: techniques</title><link>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-09-28-5be8bdace887aacodeforces5dhowtocomeupwiththesolutions3atechniques/</link><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2015 16:04:00 +0000</pubDate><author>hust.111qqz@gmail.com (111qqz)</author><guid>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-09-28-5be8bdace887aacodeforces5dhowtocomeupwiththesolutions3atechniques/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;As I work with students I often face the situation when if a problem doesn&amp;rsquo;t seem clear to a student at the first sight, it makes them unable to solve it. Indeed, you always hear about specific methods and techniques. But you don&amp;rsquo;t hear about how to think in order to apply them. In this note I&amp;rsquo;ll try to sum up my experience of solving programming contest problems. However, some pieces of advice will also be applicable for olympiads in mathematics and your first steps in academic research.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>cf 570 A. Elections</title><link>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-08-13-cf570a-elections/</link><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2015 22:46:00 +0000</pubDate><author>hust.111qqz@gmail.com (111qqz)</author><guid>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-08-13-cf570a-elections/</guid><description/></item><item><title>cf 567 C. Geometric Progression</title><link>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-08-06-cf567c-geometricprogression/</link><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2015 07:29:00 +0000</pubDate><author>hust.111qqz@gmail.com (111qqz)</author><guid>https://111qqz.com/en/post/acm-icpc/2015/2015-08-06-cf567c-geometricprogression/</guid><description/></item><item><title>cf #309a A - Kyoya and Photobooks</title><link>https://111qqz.com/